.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt DSA_SET_METHOD 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm DSA_set_default_method ,
.Nm DSA_get_default_method ,
.Nm DSA_set_method ,
.Nm DSA_new_method ,
.Nm DSA_OpenSSL
.Nd select DSA method
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/dsa.h
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 3.0, and can
be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft void
.Fo DSA_set_default_method
.Fa "const DSA_METHOD *meth"
.Fc
.Ft const DSA_METHOD *
.Fo DSA_get_default_method
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo DSA_set_method
.Fa "DSA *dsa"
.Fa "const DSA_METHOD *meth"
.Fc
.Ft DSA *
.Fo DSA_new_method
.Fa "ENGINE *engine"
.Fc
.Ft const DSA_METHOD *
.Fo DSA_OpenSSL
.Fa void
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
All of the functions described on this page are deprecated.
Applications should providers instead of method overrides.
.Pp
A
.Sy DSA_METHOD
specifies the functions that OpenSSL uses for DSA operations.
By modifying the method, alternative implementations such as hardware
accelerators may be used.
IMPORTANT: See the NOTES section for important information about how
these DSA API functions are affected by the use of
.Vt ENGINE
API calls.
.Pp
Initially, the default DSA_METHOD is the OpenSSL internal
implementation, as returned by
.Fn DSA_OpenSSL .
.Pp
.Fn DSA_set_default_method
makes
.Fa meth
the default method for all DSA structures created later.
.Sy NB :
This is true only whilst no ENGINE has been set as a default for DSA, so
this function is no longer recommended.
This function is not thread-safe and should not be called at the same
time as other OpenSSL functions.
.Pp
.Fn DSA_get_default_method
returns a pointer to the current default DSA_METHOD. However, the
meaningfulness of this result is dependent on whether the ENGINE API is
being used, so this function is no longer recommended.
.Pp
.Fn DSA_set_method
selects
.Fa meth
to perform all operations using the key
.Sy rsa .
This will replace the DSA_METHOD used by the DSA key and if the previous
method was supplied by an ENGINE, the handle to that ENGINE will be
released during the change.
It is possible to have DSA keys that only work with certain DSA_METHOD
implementations (e.g.
from an ENGINE module that supports embedded hardware-protected keys),
and in such cases attempting to change the DSA_METHOD for the key can
have unexpected results.
See
.Xr DSA_meth_new 3
for information on constructing custom DSA_METHOD objects;
.Pp
.Fn DSA_new_method
allocates and initializes a DSA structure so that
.Fa engine
will be used for the DSA operations.
If
.Fa engine
is NULL, the default engine for DSA operations is used, and if no
default ENGINE is set, the DSA_METHOD controlled by
.Fn DSA_set_default_method
is used.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn DSA_OpenSSL
and
.Fn DSA_get_default_method
return pointers to the respective
.Sy DSA_METHOD Ns s.
.Pp
.Fn DSA_set_default_method
returns no value.
.Pp
.Fn DSA_set_method
returns nonzero if the provided
.Fa meth
was successfully set as the method for
.Fa dsa
(including unloading the ENGINE handle if the previous method was
supplied by an ENGINE).
.Pp
.Fn DSA_new_method
returns NULL and sets an error code that can be obtained by
.Xr ERR_get_error 3
if the allocation fails.
Otherwise it returns a pointer to the newly allocated structure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr DSA_new 3 ,
.Xr DSA_new 3 ,
.Xr DSA_meth_new 3
.Sh HISTORY
All of these functions were deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
